# OS Hardening Techniques

## Project Overview
This project is based on a cybersecurity training exercise. It focuses on identifying suspicious website activity, reviewing network traffic, and recommending security improvements.

## Tools Used
- tcpdump
- Sandbox environment

## What I Worked On
- Identified HTTP traffic using tcpdump logs.
- Reviewed DNS queries and IP address responses.
- Analyzed TCP connection handshakes.
- Identified HTTP GET requests.
- Observed communication between two different websites.
- Reviewed possible brute-force attack activity.
- Recommended security improvements.

## Key Findings
The network logs showed that the computer initially connected to `yummyrecipesforme.com` and later communicated with `greatrecipesforme.com`.

This supported the reported website redirection during the investigation.

## Security Recommendations
- Use strong and unique passwords.
- Enable multi-factor authentication (MFA).
- Limit repeated failed login attempts.
- Monitor administrator login activity.
- Prevent the reuse of default passwords.

## Skills Practiced
- Network traffic analysis
- DNS analysis
- TCP connection analysis
- HTTP traffic inspection
- Basic incident investigation
- Security recommendations

## Project Documentation
The PDF report contains the incident summary, packet-log analysis, key findings, and recommended security improvements.
